---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Terminal UI"
  description="Use the OpenTUI client: sessions, slash commands, themes, reviews, and keyboard shortcuts."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / TUI</p>
    <h1>
      Drive Veasel
      <br />
      <em>from the terminal.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The bundled OpenTUI client talks to the local loopback API. Sessions,
      reviews, and settings stay on your machine.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Home and sessions</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <kbd>j</kbd> / <kbd>k</kbd> or arrows move the session list; Enter
          opens; <kbd>n</kbd> starts a session when the list is empty.
        </li>
        <li>
          Long lists keep the selection on screen and show a position such as{" "}
          <code>8/20</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Esc cancels a running turn. Session history and events live in local
          SQLite.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Credentials and models</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <code>/connect</code> — paste an API key, save it locally, pick a
          model (happy path).
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>s</kbd> or <code>/models</code> — full settings: endpoint
          (Ctrl+U), output budget (Ctrl+O), and model discovery.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keys are stored under{" "}
          <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/model-settings.json</code> with owner-only
          POSIX permissions (plaintext at rest). Saved profile keys win over
          environment variables for the same provider.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Themes</h2>
      <p>
        Use <code>/theme</code> to switch among <code>mint</code>,{" "}
        <code>ember</code>, <code>slate</code>, <code>mono</code>, and{" "}
        <code>aurora</code>. The default mint theme matches the product mock
        (charcoal panels, mint accents, LOCAL cue).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Reviews and slash commands</h2>
      <p>
        Type <code>/</code> for suggestions. Common flows:
      </p>
      <pre><code>/patches
/patch show &lt;id&gt;
/patch approve &lt;id&gt;   # or reject

/commands
/command show &lt;id&gt;
/command approve &lt;id&gt;

/mcp add stdio &lt;name&gt; &lt;command&gt; [args…]
/mcp add http &lt;name&gt; &lt;url&gt;
/mcp enable|disable|remove &lt;name&gt;
/mcp trust configured/&lt;name&gt;
/mcp calls
/mcp call show &lt;id&gt;
/mcp call approve &lt;id&gt;

/skills [filter]
/skill on|off &lt;name&gt;
/plugin add|remove &lt;path&gt;
/map
/usage</code></pre>
      <p>
        File edits, shell, and MCP never take effect until you inspect and
        approve. User-scoped MCP config persists in{" "}
        <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/mcp-servers.json</code>; trust is still
        per-session. Rejected or interrupted work is not replayed automatically.
        See the <a href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>MCP guide</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Usage</h2>
      <p>
        <code>/usage</code> shows provider-reported token totals when adapters
        set <code>usage.reported</code>. Veasel does not invent cost figures.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>
        Configure providers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/skills/`}>
        Skills and plugins <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>
        MCP servers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
